      "id": "narrative",
      "text": "The old lighthouse keeper climbed the spiral staircase each evening, carrying a lantern that cast long shadows across the stone walls. He had performed this ritual for forty years, ever since the automated systems had failed during the great storm. The sea below crashed against the rocks with a rhythm that matched his breathing, and he found comfort in the predictability of waves and wind. Tonight, however, something was different. A strange light flickered on the horizon, pulsing with an irregular beat that made him uneasy.",
